course: dictionary
lesson: 15040
title: Hitting back: retaliation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Retaliation means doing something bad to someone because they did something bad to you. It is another word for hitting back, a kind of revenge. «After Sam pushed Ravi off the bench, Ravi pushed him back in retaliation.» The words in retaliation show that Ravi's push was a reply to Sam's push.
explain: Use the clues around the word to check. First something bad happened, then someone did something bad back. Ask yourself: did one person hit back at another? If yes, retaliation fits. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Ravi pushed him back because Sam had pushed first» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Stories and history use this word a lot. «The soldiers marched to the border in retaliation for the attack.» A war can start with one attack and then a retaliation, and each side hits back at the other.
explain: At school, retaliation is still wrong, even when you feel angry. «Lily was teased, but she told her teacher instead of teasing back.» Telling a teacher is the right choice. Some children stay quiet because of a fear of retaliation, which means they are scared the other person will hit back.
fact: Retaliation means doing something bad to someone because they did something bad to you.
fact: Retaliation is another word for hitting back, and it is a kind of revenge.
fact: «In retaliation for» means as a reply to something bad that was done first.
fact: In a football match, a player can be sent off for retaliation, even if the other player started it.
fact: At school, the right answer to being hurt is to tell a teacher, not to hit back.
exercise: «The king sent soldiers to the border in retaliation for the attack.» Why did the king send soldiers? | To go on a holiday | To build a new bridge | *To hit back after an attack
exercise: Sam says, «Ravi pushed me, so I'm going to push him back to get even.» What is Sam planning? | An apology | *Retaliation | Sharing his lunch | A quiet walk home
exercise: Someone teases you at school. What is the right thing to do instead of retaliation? | Hit them back | Tease them back | *Tell a teacher | Ignore the rules and run away
test: «Lily did not tell anyone, because she had a fear of retaliation.» What does fear of retaliation mean? | Wanting a big prize | Liking to tell stories | *Being scared that someone will hit back | Feeling tired after lunch
test: Which sentence uses retaliation correctly? | *He kicked back in retaliation after the other boy kicked him first | He ran home in retaliation for the rain | He shared his crisps in retaliation
exam: What is the best word for hitting back after someone has hurt you? | *Retaliation | Generosity | Kindness | Patience
